holiday-display
===============

A front-yard holiday LED display: a 6 ft x 4 ft frame of 54 x 36 WS2812B pixels, homemade with the kids.
Halloween first (target 2026-10-31), then other holidays.

Layout
  notes.txt      design decisions, and proposals not yet decided
  agents/        work by Michael's agents (see below)
    sim/         pixelframe.py: a simulated frame in plain Python (draw, save a PNG of the LEDs, estimate
                 current); jack.py draws the jack-o'-lantern with it (python3 jack.py -> jack.png, jack.txt)

agents/
  Agents commit there under their own names, at will.  They clean up that history when Michael asks.
  Everything else in the repo is committed by Michael.  Only Michael pushes.
